            "result_text": "Done! The regex has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\n**How it works:**\n\n- **`^.*?`** - Starts at the beginning of a line, matching any characters non-greedily\n- **IPv4 validation** - Matches octets (0-255) separated by dots, with word boundaries (`(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])...(?![a-zA-Z0-9])`)\n- **Last date capture** - Matches the date in the capturing group `(...)` with:\n  - Month-specific day ranges (31/30/29 days)\n  - Word boundaries preventing partial matches like \"1134-12-1234\"\n- **`(?![^\\n]*DATE_PATTERN)`** - Negative lookahead ensuring no additional valid dates follow on the same line\n- **MULTILINE mode** - `^` and `$` match line boundaries, preventing cross-line matches\n\nThe regex will work with your Python code using `re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)`."
